@flexiarg inbox-zero/generated-by-role
@title Decide A Generated File's Fate By Its Role, Not Its Extension
@keywords generated, intermediate, deliverable, evidence, rebuildable-view, role-manifest, tracked
@audience repo maintainers, build authors, inbox-zero classifiers
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7, from Joe's distinction: ".aux we should probably never commit; .pdf sometimes we should"; census of tracked generated files the same day; not implemented)
@references [inbox-zero/classify-the-dirt inbox-zero/ignore-by-kind inbox-zero/promote-at-turn-end]
@see-also inbox-zero/measure-against-the-remote
@why generated files fit none of the three dirt classes when they are tracked, and the extension does not say what to do: p4ng tracks LaTeX intermediates (main.aux, main.bbl, main.blg, main.out, .fls, .fdb_latexmk) that no one should commit, and nineteen PDFs of which some are deliverables (corneli2026submitted.pdf) and some are rebuilt figures; futon2's 268 tracked .log files are run cassettes (data/wm-step/w1/steps/*/cassette.log) — evidence — not build logs. The same extension carries opposite remedies.
@how give every generated path kind a declared role, once per kind, in a per-repo role manifest (the same once-per-kind judgement as inbox-zero/ignore-by-kind), then act by role: INTERMEDIATE — a build byproduct read only by the next run of the same build (.aux, .bbl, .fls, .fdb_latexmk, LaTeX .log/.out): never commit; ignore by kind; untrack if tracked. REBUILDABLE VIEW — regenerated from committed sources on every build and read by the build or re-published (generated sections, issue boards, status infographics): either untrack and generate at build time, or commit atomically with the source change and generator run that produced it; never left modified. DELIVERABLE — consumed by someone who will not rebuild it (a submitted paper, a released figure): commit at the declared release moment with the source sha it was built from, not on every rebuild. EVIDENCE — produced by a run and cited or pinned by a record (cassettes, receipts, run logs): commit as produced and never regenerate; this is real work, not generated noise. A generated path with no declared role is unclassifiable and reported, never guessed from its extension.
@violation-signature an ignore rule by extension that swallows evidence (*.log hiding run cassettes); a deliverable PDF recommitted on every rebuild so its history no longer marks releases; an intermediate committed because its directory was added whole; a rebuildable view left modified between builds so the tree is never clean; an evidence file regenerated so its pinned hash no longer matches.
! conclusion: A generated file's fate follows its declared role — intermediates are never committed, views are committed with their sources or not at all, deliverables at release, evidence as produced — and a path with no role is reported, not guessed.

  + context: Builds, runs and publishers write into tracked trees across the stack; many outputs were committed once by whole-directory adds and are rebuilt continuously since.

  + IF:
    A tracked or untracked file is the output of a generator rather than authored work.

  + HOWEVER:
    Extension is not role: .log is a LaTeX byproduct in one repo and a pinned run cassette in another, .pdf is a throwaway figure build in one place and a submitted paper in the next; and a rebuild leaves tracked views modified between every build, so a repo that builds often is never clean.

  + THEN:
    Declare a role per generated path kind, once, and apply the role's remedy; report generated paths with no declared role.

  + BECAUSE:
    The remedy depends on who consumes the file and whether they can regenerate it: nobody (intermediate), the build (view), a reader who will not rebuild (deliverable), or a record that pins it (evidence).

  + evidence: census 2026-09-16 of tracked files with build-byproduct extensions — futon2 418 (268 .log, 150 .out, predominantly run cassettes), futon3c 53, p4ng 40 (7 .aux, 4 .bbl, 4 .blg, 3 .fdb_latexmk, 4 .fls, 12 .log, 6 .out), futon5 16, futon3 13; tracked PDFs futon5 47, p4ng 19, futon2 6; p4ng's 2026-09-16 21:01 gate failure was nine tracked rebuildable views 40.7h modified (issue-board.edn/html and sec-issue-board-generated.tex, which build-p4ng.sh already pins together by sha, plus other sec-*-generated.tex, war-room-tetrahedron.svg, wm-status.pdf).

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Joe declares the role manifest for p4ng first (which PDFs are deliverables; whether generated sections are committed with their build or generated at build time).
